This is original C.  It carries no historical source, and no release tree,
tool binary, or emulator is vendored into it.

Two parts are nevertheless derived work in the sense that matters for
attribution.  The filesystem writer core (src/s5fs_core.c) is a host port of
2.9BSD's cmd/mkfs.c, following the original's layout arithmetic, free-list
interleave, allocator and inode/directory writers closely enough to reproduce
its output; and the on-disk structural constants (src/pdp11fs.h) come from the
2.9BSD headers.  The 2.9BSD sources those derive from carry no copyright notice
of their own -- only an SCCS id -- and are covered by the Berkeley terms above
as Regents of the University of California work, while the underlying Research
Unix content falls under the Caldera ancient-Unix license.
